BUNDLED GECKO IOT CLIENT

The client under custom_components/gecko/gecko_iot_client originates from
https://github.com/geckoal/gecko-iot-client, commit
b799e0cef27099b18d87f52be359353d7ec53c1e (v1.0.3).
Its GPL-3.0-or-later license is preserved in that directory as LICENSE.
The integration LICENSE continues to describe the integration source.
Local changes relocate imports, identify the bundled source, and repair models,
command delivery and MQTT configuration. See docs/RESTORATION.md and the README
for source attribution and community changes.

STANDALONE BUILD PREPARATION

The same client sources can now be built as the unpublished development package
gecko-intouch3-client, version 3.0.0.dev0. The import package remains
gecko_iot_client; the current custom integration still uses its bundled relative
namespace. Package metadata preserves the inherited client license. This does
not change source ownership or establish license approval for core inclusion.

EXTRACTED INTEGRATION HELPERS

The modules under gecko_iot_client/helpers originate from the Apache-2.0
licensed community HA integration, based on Gecko Alliance's official
integration (aaf94de). They retain Apache-2.0, documented per file, and
LICENSE-APACHE is included. They have not been relicensed as GPL source.
The original client sources retain their inherited GPL-3.0-or-later license.

Helper contributions/adaptations include @karlg100 (telemetry/connectivity),
@nmonteleone18 (RGB normalization), @markus-lassfolk (Waterlab/shadow
interpretation), and @dansbaker (reviewed community restoration). Source
review and detailed attribution remain in the repository README and docs.
